SUMMARY:Science Comedy Night
LOCATION:The Comedy Loft of DC\, 1523 22nd St NW\, Washington
DESCRIPTION:Science Comedy Night is back with comedians\, experts\, and peo
 ple who still Google their symptoms at 2 a.m. for an evening of jokes with 
 a health science twist. Expect sharp stand-up\, strange medical facts from 
 across the animal kingdom\, and enough humor to make your high school biolo
 gy teacher proud—or deeply concerned.\n\nPerformers include headliner Ben
  Miller (Edinburgh Fringe Festival\, NY Comedy Festival)\, Kasha Patel (fou
 nder of DC Science Comedy\, NPR)\, and some surprise guests. The show will 
 include an unhinged Q&A with a licensed medical professional who will answe
 r audience questions.\nSide effects may include sore (face) cheeks\, elevat
 ed heart rate\, sudden (legal) snorting\, and an uncontrollable urge to say
 \, “Actually\, that’s fascinating.”\nAnyone with a body and brain can
  enjoy this show\, regardless of scientific background. Book your tickets b
 efore they become statistically unavailable.\nWarning: this event has not b
 een approved by the FDA\, peer-reviewed\, or shown to improve long-term sur
 vival—but it may cause acute laughter and temporary faith in humanity.\n\
 nAbout Ben Miller: Ben Miller is an NYC based scientist turned comedian who
  has been working for the past 10 years at comedy clubs\, museums and volca
 noes across the world. In 2022\, Ben Miller's debut hour\, Stand-Up Science
 \, had a completely sold-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe Festival and toure
 d 50+ cities internationally. In 2023\, he was an Artist in Residence at Ha
 wai’i Volcanoes National Park\, the first stand-up comedian ever selected
  by the National Parks Arts Foundation. This year\, he is bringing his late
 st hilarious special on all things health science.\n\nAbout DC Science Come
 dy: DC Science Comedy is a comedy production company founded and hosted by 
 journalist and stand-up comedian Kasha Patel\, who also travels around the 
 country for solo science comedy performances. Patel has traveled around the
  country with the show and has been featured on NPR\, TED\, BBC\, and The W
 ashington Post. The goal of our…\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/come
 dy-atlas/event/science-comedy-night/
